NullIME

The Japanese dictionary assets (nullime-ja.dict, nullime-ja.small.dict) are
not in this repository. tools/nullime-dict builds them from the Mozc OSS
dictionary (https://github.com/google/mozc, commit
a4541df29db443b49f81cf54665873b68fde9efa, src/data/dictionary_oss). Anyone
redistributing a built asset redistributes that data under the notices
below; each asset also carries the dictionary's README.txt notices in its
license section.

The engine embeds four language-model tables,
crates/nullime-engine/data/ko_syllable.bin, ko_particle.txt,
en_trigram.bin and ja_bigram.bin, built by
tools/nullime-dict/gen_lm.py from the sources below. They hold quantized
frequency statistics; ko_particle.txt also lists the particle forms from
the survey's 조사 list. No sentences from the sources are included.

ja_bigram.bin is a hiragana bigram derived from the readings in the Mozc
dictionary above (src/data/dictionary_oss/dictionary00.txt to
dictionary09.txt, same commit), under the Mozc, IPAdic and Okinawa
dictionary notices below. It holds no entries, only quantized
reading-bigram statistics.

===============================================================================
Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org)

ko_syllable.bin and en_trigram.bin are derived from Tatoeba's Korean and
English sentence exports
(https://downloads.tatoeba.org/exports/per_language/kor/kor_sentences.tsv.bz2,
https://downloads.tatoeba.org/exports/per_language/eng/eng_sentences.tsv.bz2).
Sentences by Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org) contributors, licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France (CC BY 2.0 FR,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/). The tables are a
modified (statistically derived) form of that work.

